 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "현재진행형 am / is / are + -ing",
   "en": "Present continuous: am / is / are + -ing"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "지금 이 순간 일어나는 일은 am / is / are + 동사-ing로 말합니다. 부정은 be 뒤에 not, 의문문은 be를 앞으로 보냅니다. e로 끝나는 동사는 e를 빼고 -ing를 붙이고(write → writing), 짧은 동사는 자음을 겹칩니다(run → running).",
   "en": "Talk about what is happening at this moment with am / is / are + verb-ing. For a negative add 'not' after 'be'; for a question put 'be' first. Verbs ending in -e drop the e (write → writing); short verbs double the last consonant (run → running)."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "규칙 / Rule",
    "원형 / Base",
    "-ing"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "+ -ing",
     "work",
     "working"
    ],
    [
     "e 삭제 + -ing",
     "write",
     "writing"
    ],
    [
     "자음 겹침 + -ing",
     "run",
     "running"
    ],
    [
     "자음 겹침 + -ing",
     "sit",
     "sitting"
    ],
    [
     "+ -ing",
     "listen",
     "listening"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "지금을 나타내는 말: now, at the moment, today.",
    "en": "Time words for now: now, at the moment, today."
   },
   {
    "ko": "be동사는 주어에 맞게: I am, she is, they are.",
    "en": "'Be' agrees with the subject: I am, she is, they are."
   },
   {
    "ko": "know, like, want 같은 상태 동사는 진행형으로 잘 쓰지 않습니다.",
    "en": "State verbs such as know, like and want are not normally used in the continuous."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
